		// command and nothing could order them, so an unplaced claim may name
		// an agent NEARER than whatever the source records. The owner check
		// below is strictly weaker than the resolver's — HasAncestor asks
		// "is this an ancestor at all", never "is this the nearest" — so
		// letting it run here would answer a question the resolver
		// deliberately declined, and would do it silently.
		return false, "several agent sessions claim this command and none could be ordered, so none of them can be confirmed as its caller"
	}

