	// have used it: ResolveCallerSession resolves against the CURRENT
	// repository's session store, so in a cross-repository adoption the source
	// state — and the owner recorded on it — was never in the listing it
	// searched. For an agent that publishes a session ID that gap is
	// invisible, because the environment names the source session directly and
	// matches above. For Gemini CLI and opencode, which publish nothing,
	// ancestry is all there is and it was looking in the wrong store: their
	// own cross-repo adoption — the case the command exists for — would be
	// refused, with --allow-foreign-session as the only way through, teaching
	// agents to waive a real check in order to do a legitimate thing.
